00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.020
The theme for this
year's celebration

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.560
is Truth and Power:
Students Leading for Change.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.480
We're here this
morning to celebrate

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.550
life and legacy of
Dr. King, but also

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.500
to reflect on the question,
what can and should

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.630
be done in the face of
systematic injustice.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.970
Individual actions
can make a difference,

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.210
but do they add up
to something more?

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.160
How can we work together
for broader and deeper

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.070
social changes?

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.910
Dr. King was able to
mobilize a generation

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.730
to challenge [? Reese's ?]
Laws and practices

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:40.390
through civil disobedience
and collective action.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:42.240
It is our turn now.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.610
What is the next step?

